# Fibonacci Shader — a Skia RuntimeEffect (SkSL) drawing N glowing points on a
# Fibonacci sphere, animated by a ping-pong iTime; a slider sets N (5..350
# iterations of the shader loop) and the wand button randomises the angle
# multiplier.
# What this test covers: dragging N to the maximum (heaviest shader: 350 loop
# iterations per pixel) and holding it while time animates, past both ends of
# the slider (clamp), a slow scrub, the wand button single + rapid presses
# (uniform changes while N is high and low), and back to the minimum.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/fibonacci-shader"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait "label=\"🪄\"" 10000
wait 1500
# Slider thumb starts at x=40 (track 40..361, y=583). Drag to max and beyond.
gesture pan 40 583 345 0 900
wait 1000
gesture pan 345 583 50 0 400
wait 2500
press "label=\"🪄\""
wait 1500
press 310 722 --count 6 --interval-ms 150
wait 2000
# Slow scrub down to the middle, then past the start.
gesture pan 361 583 -160 0 2500
wait 1000
press "label=\"🪄\""
wait 1000
gesture pan 200 583 -195 0 600
wait 800
gesture pan 45 583 -40 0 400
wait 1000
press "label=\"🪄\""
wait 1500
# Quick flicks on the thumb from the min.
gesture pan 40 583 120 0 150
gesture pan 140 583 -120 0 150
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
